1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:01,304
Welcome back!

2
00:00:01,304 --> 00:00:03,406
Missed calls are missed customers.

3
00:00:03,406 --> 00:00:08,166
In this lesson, we'll set up a Voice AI
receptionist that answers your phone,

4
00:00:08,166 --> 00:00:12,618
books appointments, and puts urgent
calls straight through to your team.

5
00:00:13,482 --> 00:00:15,708
Go to AI Agents, then Voice AI.

6
00:00:15,708 --> 00:00:18,365
Voice AI is included on the Pro plan.

7
00:00:18,365 --> 00:00:22,961
At the top, you can see how your
agent is doing: calls answered,

8
00:00:22,961 --> 00:00:26,049
appointments booked,
and calls transferred.

9
00:00:26,049 --> 00:00:28,203
Bloom's agent is called Rosie.

10
00:00:28,203 --> 00:00:29,280
Let's open her.

11
00:00:30,130 --> 00:00:32,694
Under Agent goals, start with the voice.

12
00:00:32,694 --> 00:00:34,488
Press play to hear each one.

13
00:00:34,488 --> 00:00:36,732
Pick a voice that suits your brand.

14
00:00:36,732 --> 00:00:39,167
Bloom uses Emma, a warm British voice.

15
00:00:40,018 --> 00:00:43,436
Next, the greeting: the first
thing every caller hears.

16
00:00:43,436 --> 00:00:47,662
Keep it short and friendly, and
always say it's a virtual assistant.

17
00:00:47,662 --> 00:00:51,825
Callers appreciate the honesty,
and it sets the right expectations.

18
00:00:52,676 --> 00:00:53,713
Then the prompt.

19
00:00:53,713 --> 00:00:58,706
Tell Rosie who she is, and list her
goals in order: answer questions from the

20
00:00:58,706 --> 00:01:02,401
knowledge base, book new
patients, transfer urgent calls,

21
00:01:02,401 --> 00:01:04,282
and otherwise take a message.

22
00:01:04,282 --> 00:01:07,135
Add rules, like never
giving medical advice.

23
00:01:07,985 --> 00:01:12,582
Under Phone and availability,
choose which number Rosie answers.

24
00:01:12,582 --> 00:01:14,522
Then set her working hours.

25
00:01:14,522 --> 00:01:19,191
Bloom has her on from 7am until
10pm, so she catches early calls,

26
00:01:19,191 --> 00:01:21,992
lunchtime rushes and evening enquiries.

27
00:01:22,841 --> 00:01:24,186
Now the Actions tab.

28
00:01:24,186 --> 00:01:27,480
Call transfer routes
callers to the right person.

29
00:01:27,480 --> 00:01:30,303
A dental emergency goes straight to Sarah.

30
00:01:30,303 --> 00:01:32,320
Billing questions go to Priya.

31
00:01:32,320 --> 00:01:35,480
And anyone who asks for
a person goes to James.

32
00:01:36,330 --> 00:01:41,478
Turn on Appointment booking, so Rosie can
book callers straight into your calendars.

33
00:01:41,478 --> 00:01:46,197
And with Send SMS after the call, every
caller gets a friendly text with your

34
00:01:46,197 --> 00:01:46,994
booking link.

35
00:01:47,844 --> 00:01:50,083
Finally, keep your team in the loop.

36
00:01:50,083 --> 00:01:54,187
Rosie saves a summary and transcript
of every call to the contact,

37
00:01:54,187 --> 00:01:56,551
and can email the summary to you, too.

38
00:01:57,404 --> 00:02:02,250
Before going live, click Test agent,
and have a real conversation with Rosie,

39
00:02:02,250 --> 00:02:03,634
right in your browser.

40
00:02:03,634 --> 00:02:07,913
Ask the questions your customers
ask, and listen to how she answers.

41
00:02:08,764 --> 00:02:13,196
Once Rosie is live, every call
appears in Call logs, with who called,

42
00:02:13,196 --> 00:02:15,637
how long it lasted, and what happened.

43
00:02:15,637 --> 00:02:20,134
This morning, Olivia called about
Invisalign, and Rosie booked her in.

44
00:02:20,134 --> 00:02:22,318
Click the call to see the details.

45
00:02:23,172 --> 00:02:27,531
Here's the call summary, the actions
Rosie took, and the full transcript.

46
00:02:27,531 --> 00:02:29,800
Press play to listen to the recording.

47
00:02:29,800 --> 00:02:33,741
It's the quickest way to check
she's saying exactly what you want.

48
00:02:34,591 --> 00:02:35,659
Here's a pro tip.

49
00:02:35,659 --> 00:02:37,794
Listen to Rosie's first ten calls.

50
00:02:37,794 --> 00:02:40,747
Whenever she hesitates
or gets something wrong,

51
00:02:40,747 --> 00:02:44,452
add the answer to your knowledge
base, or tweak her prompt.

52
00:02:44,452 --> 00:02:46,965
A few small fixes make a big difference.

53
00:02:47,836 --> 00:02:50,712
Your phone is now
answered around the clock!

54
00:02:50,712 --> 00:02:55,549
In the next lesson, we'll use Content
AI to write emails and social posts,

55
00:02:55,549 --> 00:02:57,509
and create images, in seconds.

56
00:02:57,509 --> 00:02:58,425
See you there.
